google.com>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Dimitri Glazkov <dglazkov@chromium.org>, \"Philip Jägenstedt\" <foolip@chromium.org>, Jan-Ivar Bruaroey <wingboy@gmail.com>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Mounir Lamouri <mounir@lamouri.fr>, Renganathan Ramamoorthy <renganathan@chromium.org>, Raymond Toy <rtoy@chromium.org>, Ben Wells <benwells@chromium.org>"}]}}]},{"messages":[{"snippet":"I&#39;m trying to understand how the Chrome content layer works, specifically how content_shell gets","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Subject","value":"[blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"From","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 7 Jun 2016 12:36:49 -0400"},{"name":"To","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Both processes run the same binary. There isn&#39;t a browser process app and a renderer process app.","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"\"Torne (Richard Coles)\" <torne@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 07 Jun 2016 16:50:36 +0000"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"To","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"On Tue, Jun 7, 2016 at 12:36 PM, Andy Somogyi &lt;andy.somogyi@gmail.com&gt; wrote: I&#39;m still a","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Avi Drissman <avi@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 7 Jun 2016 13:06:59 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"To","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Thanks, that makes a lot more sense now. What about OpenGL canvas, or video element, or plugins like","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"From","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 8 Jun 2016 02:41:24 -0400"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Avi Drissman <avi@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"On analyzing the multi process architecture further, I just don&#39;t think it will work for my needs","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"From","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 8 Jun 2016 04:06:26 -0400"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Avi Drissman <avi@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Single-process mode is only regularly used/tested in Android WebView (and some tests). On other OSes/","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"\"Torne (Richard Coles)\" <torne@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 08 Jun 2016 09:01:24 +0000"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"To","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>, Avi Drissman <avi@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"On Wed, Jun 8, 2016 at 2:41 AM, Andy Somogyi &lt;andy.somogyi@gmail.com&gt; wrote: What about OpenGL","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Avi Drissman <avi@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 8 Jun 2016 10:57:25 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"To","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"As other posters have noted, single-process model is unsupported for desktop. Anyways, I don&#39;t","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 08 Jun 2016 20:53:17 +0000"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] chrome content API"},{"name":"To","value":"Andy Somogyi <andy.somogyi@gmail.com>, Avi Drissman <avi@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Hi Stefan, First off, I&#39;ve only been studying t