Tapuska' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Thu, 23 Jun 2016 10:01:05 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Malte Ubl <malteubl@google.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Fwiw removing this did break the autocomplete in Chrome&#39;s codereview tool as I said: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=632932 and execCommand doesn&#39;t appear to work on input","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 2 Aug 2016 22:41:14 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Wait, but Firefox does not fire the default action for non-click events, if I remember correctly. I guess the underlying issue (in your case) here is that Chrome does not add value changes triggered by","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 18:48:49 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"I think this specific default action (adding to the undo stack) should just be whitelisted. Does anyone think that programmatically modifying the undo stack is harmful? And if so, why is it fine for","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 19:03:19 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"I don&#39;t think it&#39;s acceptable to stop running execCommand against input and textarea. That completely breaks inserting text with the undo stack and was explicitly given as the workaround and a","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 09:18:35 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, yosin@chromium.org, Ojan Vafai <ojan@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Yep, I agree that input events (textInput or the standard input) should just trigger undo stack modification. ☆PhistucK On Wed, Aug 3, 2016 at 7:18 PM, Elliott Sprehn &lt;esprehn@chromium.org&gt; wrote","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 19:22:11 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Yoshifumi Inoue <yosin@chromium.org>, Ojan Vafai <ojan@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"I agree that &quot;execCommand&quot; against input / textarea should be retained. We indeed needs &quot;void open();&quot; and &quot;void close();&quot; for &lt;select&gt; if untrusted mousedown events","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Sun, 7 Aug 2016 03:13:47 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"gongdh11@gmail.com"},{"name":"To","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"dtapuska@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"}]}},{"snippet":"In terms of the open, close etc. It was discussed that because of the really low usage of executing the default action for untrusted events. If people wanted this they could build their own custom","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"\"'Dave Tapuska' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Thu, 11 Aug 2016 11:53:08 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"gongdh11@gmail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}}]},{"messages":[{"snippet":"Contacts Eng: groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org PM: laforge@chromium.org Target Q4 2016","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 9 May 2016 15:34:26 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"From","value":"Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"(Adding blink-dev) Why would YouTube need Flash? Oh, the video manager? Can you work with them in","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 09:59:31 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[blink-dev] Re: [chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"On Tue, 10 May 2016 at 17:00 PhistucK &lt;phistuck@gmail.com&gt; wrote: (Adding blink-dev) Why would","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Matt Giuca <mgiuca@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 07:04:21 +0000"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Re: [chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>, Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Sorry for not watching the slides - I am simply firewalled here, so I cannot access Google Drive","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 10:07:51 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Re: [chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"Matt Giuca <mgiuca@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"On Monday, May 9, 2016 at 5:35:28 PM UTC-5, Anthony LaForge wrote: Presentation HTML5 by Default","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Fri, 13 May 2016 20:21:06 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"B Galliart <bgallia@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"May I kindly ask what is the long term goal for the Chromium team? Will you be satisfied with this","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 00:54:02 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Ruben Gerlach' via Chromium-dev\" <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"While you may not get an official answer, it is obvious (to me, anyway) that the plan is to eliminate","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 11:07:42 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Thanks for your reply. I would like to avoid a Flash vs HTML5 discussion, but let me say this: Our","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 02:10:16 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Ruben Gerlach' via Chromium-dev\" <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"Note that only the browser option will be impacted. You could still redirect your users to install","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 12:58:35 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"While I agree that the writing has been on the wall for a long time now, and this kind of move should","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 03:04:16 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"Richard Davey <rdavey@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"I would like to add two thoughts: 1) HTML5 is a great tool for building websites, but it is a not so","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 03:31:03 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Ruben Gerlach' via Chromium-dev\" <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"I don&#39;t like this. On Tuesday, 10 May 2016 01:35:28 UTC+3, Anthony LaForge wrote: Contacts Eng:","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 04:28:25 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"radu birsan <radu.flash@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"If you read any IT news in the last few years it has been pretty obvious that Flash is phasing out,","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 04:41:02 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"Thaek <daniel.manser@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"If you Google &#39;top facebook games&#39;, and you browse to each one, you will find a majority of","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 06:33:31 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"Arianit Uka <auka@bigvikinggames.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"If you read the proposal it doesn&#39;t advocate the removal of Flash Player at all. In fact it","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 14:47:46 +0100"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"From","value":"Richard Davey <rdavey@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"auka@bigvikinggames.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"}]}},{"snippet":"step by step google moving to completely remove flash player from Chrome. IMHO On Monday, May 16,","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 07:04:20 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"Vakhtangi Beridze <22round@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"auka@bigvikinggames.com, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"Richard: Apart from the fact that adding another layer or approval will decrease user retention and","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 07:33:42 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Ruben Gerlach' via Chromium-dev\" <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"auka@bigvikinggames.com, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"I agree 100%. But that isn&#39;t what _this_ proposal is about. Photon Storm Ltd. http://www.","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 15:35:20 +0100"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"From","value":"Richard Davey <rdavey@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"22round@gmail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, auka@bigvikinggames.com, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"}]}},{"snippet":"I don&#39;t believe the Facebook feed uses Flash, I&#39;m pretty sure it&#39;s just their games. If","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 07:50:51 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"James Welbes <james.welbes@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"I&#39;m not sure how much thoughts have been put in this &quot;rough draft&quot; proposal but here","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 08:02:05 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"zwetan kjukov <zwetan@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"On Mon, May 16, 2016 at 6:02 PM, zwetan kjukov &lt;zwetan@gmail.com&gt; wrote: Highjacking a URL","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 18:23:57 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"zwetan@gmail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet"